  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BA3-QA1-008" ;
  triage:title "tick_once runs queue-drain before owed-task-starts, the reverse of the sprint doc's documented tick order" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-1 (req-qa), PR #1402 @ c13f9bddf, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1402#issuecomment-5643113496. Tick order in tick_once runs queue-drain before owed-task-starts, the reverse of the sprint doc's documented sequence (observations -> owed starts -> drain -> dispose). The two passes touch disjoint populations so this is likely benign, but doc and code should agree. fenix's ruling (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1402#issuecomment-5643134050): STANDS, minor -- code must follow the doc's tick order; reorder in BA3-FIX-R3-1789183410, or state why the doc is wrong before touching it." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ordering-defect" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
